# Git and environments (user decisions 2026-10-22 and 2026-10-24)

Full rules: `docs/agents/git-workflow.md`.

- GitHub has one permanent branch, `main` (production). Each batch of work happens on a short-lived branch that becomes a pull request into `main`; GitHub deletes the branch after it merges. `dev` is retired; never recreate it.
- Flow: branch from the latest `main` → verify locally (`scripts/verify.sh`) → open or update the pull request (`scripts/land.sh`) → the user tests it locally and merges it.
- Never push to `main`. Never merge a pull request unless the user asks. Never force-push. Never delete `main`.
- Every pull request into `main` uses the plain-language template: New features added, Improvements, Bug Fixes.
- Vercel deploys only `main`; preview deployments are disabled. Pull requests into `main` run CI. Local verification remains required.
- To catch a branch up with `main`, merge `origin/main` into it (`scripts/land.sh` does this). Never rebase a branch that is already on GitHub.
- Local servers: web on port 3000, engine on port 8000, nothing else (`scripts/local-app.sh`). If busy, wait for the owner; never pick another port; stop what you start.
- Children never push or open pull requests; the parent does.
